# XSH posix_spawnattr_getschedpolicy() and posix_spawnattr_setschedpolicy()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Both functions belong to the Spawn and Process Scheduling options, so the
# assertions are conditional on SPN+PS. Effects are shown by really spawning
# this program as a child image; changing the scheduler may need privilege,
# and a spawn that is refused for that reason is UNRESOLVED. The functions
# return the error number; errno is not used.

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getschedpolicy.001
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getschedpolicy.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getschedpolicy.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       SPN+PS
since      2001
says       posix_spawnattr_getschedpolicy() on a newly initialised object returns 0
           (the value stored is unspecified and not examined).
test       t/001-default.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getschedpolicy.002
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getschedpolicy.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getschedpolicy.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       SPN+PS
since      2001
says       posix_spawnattr_setschedpolicy() with the calling process's own policy
           returns 0 and posix_spawnattr_getschedpolicy() returns 0 and
           stores it; the other policies SCHED_FIFO, SCHED_RR and
           SCHED_OTHER that setschedpolicy accepts also read back
           (EINVAL accepted for them); two objects keep their own
           values.
test       t/002-roundtrip.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getschedpolicy.003
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getschedpolicy.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       SPN+PS
since      2001
says       A child spawned with POSIX_SPAWN_SETSCHEDULER and a spawn-schedpolicy
           set through posix_spawnattr_setschedpolicy() runs under that
           policy.
note       Changing the scheduler may need privilege (implementation-defined); a
           refusal is UNRESOLVED. The test asks for a real-time policy,
           which an ordinary user may be refused.
needs      root
test       t/003-effect.c
